[
  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14097781",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-124235",
      "knowledge_point_id": "0403251a-9491-5d04-ab5a-ed027024d0a4",
      "knowledge_point": "Inverting Affine Transformations Given in Matrix Form",
      "problem": "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ a & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-2\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+\\frac{3}{2}+(-\\frac{5}{2})=1.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
