  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14097781",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-124317",
      "knowledge_point_id": "b99071b9-d463-5e3e-9a0d-71711af836cb",
      "knowledge_point": "Inverting Affine Transformations Given in Parametric Form",
      "problem": "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=5v-7u+3,\\,y=7v-10u+5.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=ax-5y+4,\\,v=bx+cy+5,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$",
      "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5v-7u+3 \\\\ 7v-10u+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7u+5v \\\\ -10u+7v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -10 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{7\\cdot (-7)-5\\cdot (-10)}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ 10 & -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ 10 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ 10 & -7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ 10 & -7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x-3 \\\\ y-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7\\cdot (x-3)+(-5)\\cdot (y-5) \\\\ 10\\cdot (x-3)+(-7)\\cdot (y-5)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7x-5y+4 \\\\ 10x-7y+5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=7x-5y+4,\\,v=10x+(-7)y+5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=7+10+(-7)=10.\n$$",
