  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14098324",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-101528",
      "knowledge_point_id": "91691448-c59a-56dc-a775-d4e9c3297036",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Scalar Projection Using Components",
      "problem": "Let $a=⟨2,-1,2⟩$ and $b=⟨6,2,-3⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 6+(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-3)}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{|\\,a\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a-{\\text{comp}}_{a}\\,b & =\\frac{4}{7}-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{7}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{3}{21}-\\frac{7}{21}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{2}{7}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{4}{7}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{4}{3}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
